  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INWES-ARN Conference 2024 (ACWES 2024) Empowering African Women and Girls in STEM towards achieving the Africa we want</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Network of Women Engineers and Scientists (INWES) aims to influence policies in STEM and promote education, recruitment, and advancement of women in these fields. Establishing the INWES Africa Regional Network (ARN) in 2014 addressed the specific needs of African women in STEM. The INWES-ARN Conference (ACWES), Rwanda, 4th-8th November, 2024, will further empower African women and girls. The event, including seminars for knowledge exchange and capacity building in STEM and advocacy, will be hosted by the Rwanda Association for Women in Science &amp;amp; Engineering (RAWISE) and the African Institute for Mathematical Sciences (AIMS) in Rwanda.</narrative>
  </description>
